## Not a measured weakness of the panel: four of five §M6 checks need a real provider

Discriminative validity, acquiescence bias, position bias, and known-answer calibration all depend on the panel's output actually reflecting the artefact, the question framing, or the option position it was given. `{{ report.provider_name }}` synthesizes structured output (category, summary, agreement, choice) uniformly at random from the full prompt hash, blind to all three -- so none of these four checks produced a real number in this run. This is stated here for completeness. It is a limitation of *running this harness offline*, not a measured property of the synthetic panel, and is not counted toward the two measured weaknesses above.
