## Partially measured: one or more §M6 checks lost subjects mid-run

At least one of discriminative validity, acquiescence bias, position bias, or known-answer calibration finished with fewer subjects than it started with -- see the **Provenance**/subject-count fields in `docs/validity_report.md` for which check and how many. Every number reported for a partially-measured section is computed only over the subjects that completed every probe call for it; it is not padded, extrapolated, or presented as full-panel coverage. This is stated here for completeness, same as the not-measured-offline note above, and is not counted toward the two measured weaknesses above -- it is a property of this run's reliability, not a measured property of the synthetic panel.
