## A real, cassette-backed recording exists -- for one model configuration only

This file is always generated from a `FakeProvider` run (see the section above), because `sul validate` never constructs anything else (PROJECT_SPEC.md §M6 Deviation 5). Separately, `tests/cassettes/` holds a real, cassette-backed recording against the actual Anthropic API: 5 personas, `bad_onboarding.html`, **Persona/Moderator/probes on `claude-haiku-4-5`, Analyst on `claude-sonnet-5`** ("Config A" in PROJECT_SPEC.md §M6 Deviation 12). Discriminative validity, acquiescence bias, and position bias all came back genuinely `MEASURED` against it -- real numbers, not this file's gated placeholders.

**Those numbers describe that one configuration and do not transfer down a model tier.** The Analyst's category/severity judgments and the panel's probe replies are specific to Sonnet 5 and Haiku 4.5 respectively; a Haiku-only Analyst ("Config B") has not yet produced a completed run (§M6 Deviation 12 records why and what's still open), and nothing here should be read as validating a cheaper or different model combination. See PROJECT_SPEC.md's §M6 Deviation 12 for what was recorded, what failed, and what remains open before Config B can complete.
